cargo-zempic [VERSION]
  workspace:      [WORKSPACE_ROOT]  (1 members, 1 selected)
  profile:        release  (inherits: none)
  optimizing for: size
  target:         aarch64-apple-darwin

── TIER 1 · FOUNDATIONAL ──────────────────────────────────────────── 2 findings

  ╭ HIGH  profile/debug-info                                            moderate
  │ change    true -> false
  │ at        Cargo.toml:17  profile.release.debug
  │ cost      effort trivial · runtime none · fix safe · confidence high
  │ why       Debug information is produced and then dropped by stripping.
  │           Disabling `debug` saves compile time and the intermediate disk it
  │           writes while leaving the linked artifact largely unchanged.
  │ tradeoff  A binary built without debug information cannot be stepped
  ╰           through.

  ╭ LOW  profile/split-debuginfo                                           small
  │ change    "off" -> "packed"
  │ at        Cargo.toml:20  profile.release.split-debuginfo
  │ cost      effort trivial · runtime none · fix safe · confidence high
  │ why       On this target debug information is left in the linked artifact.
  │           Splitting it into side files moves it out without discarding it.
  │ tradeoff  This recommendation is platform-specific and the split files must
  ╰           be kept beside the binary for a debugger to find them.

SUMMARY
  2 findings: 1 high, 1 low.  By magnitude: 1 moderate, 1 small.
  2 auto-fixable.

  Magnitude is an ordinal judgement, not a measurement. zempic does not build
  and does not read compiled artifacts, so it reports no sizes.
